# Raging River with Isshin, Two Heavens as One and Adeline, Resplendent Cathar: Isshin attacks, and the River and Adeline each
# trigger twice. The first River resolves - Phyrexian Walker "left", Kobolds of Kher Keep "right", Isshin "left" - then both
# Adelines make a Human token tapped and attacking, then the second River - Kobolds of Kher Keep "left", Phyrexian Walker
# "right" - labels Isshin and both tokens "left". A token was labelled by the second resolution alone, so only the second's
# "left" pile may block it: Kobolds of Kher Keep may, Phyrexian Walker, "left" only in the first resolution's piles, which
# were made before the token was there, may not (the rulings: a creature entering attacking after a resolution is not
# restricted by it).
[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Gleemox
Mox Pearl
Mox Jet
Raging River
Isshin, Two Heavens as One
Adeline, Resplendent Cathar
Mountain x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Phyrexian Walker
Kobolds of Kher Keep
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island
Island x10

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Gleemox.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Gleemox.Activate(Color: Red)
Bot1.Hand.Raging River.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Isshin, Two Heavens as One.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Phyrexian Walker.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Kobolds of Kher Keep.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Gleemox.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Adeline, Resplendent Cathar.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Attack(Isshin, Two Heavens as One > Bot2)
Bot1.Triggers(Raging River; Adeline, Resplendent Cathar; Adeline, Resplendent Cathar; Raging River)
Bot2.Choose(Phyrexian Walker)
Bot1.Choose(Isshin, Two Heavens as One)
Bot2.Choose(Kobolds of Kher Keep)
Bot1.Choose(Isshin, Two Heavens as One; Human Token#1; Human Token#2)
Bot2.Pass
! Bot2.Block(Phyrexian Walker > Human Token)
Bot2.Block(Kobolds of Kher Keep > Human Token)
? Combat.Blocks = Kobolds of Kher Keep > Human Token

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Human Token#1.BlockRestriction = Can't be blocked except by creatures with flying and creatures in a "left" pile; Labelled by Raging River
Bot2.Battlefield.Phyrexian Walker.BlockRestriction = In the "left" pile; In the "right" pile
